# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Journals written by a local run. `EMOB_JOURNAL_DIR` defaults to `var` — a path
# somebody notices, rather than a temporary directory a reboot would empty
# without an error — and what a daemon decided on this machine is not something
# to commit.
var/

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# Internal-only documents (not published) — the architecture notes and the backlog.
#
# The third-party corpus — regulations, laws, standards, protocol documents and
# papers, copyrighted — lives at `concepts/reference/` and is covered by this line,
# indexed with retrieval URLs in `concepts/REFERENCES.md` so the folder can be rebuilt.
/concepts/

# This project's own feature specifications, and the Spec Kit machinery that
# produces them: one `specs/NNN-slug/` per change (spec, plan, tasks, the
# threatspec threat-model.yaml), `.specify/memory/constitution.md`, the threatspec
# extension, and the `/speckit-*` skills. Same rule as `concepts/` — internal.
#
# Until 2026-11-18 `specs/` held the corpus now under `concepts/reference/`; a
# stale copy is ignored by the same line. Matches hems, ocpp-kit, mako and agentplane.
/specs/
/.specify/
/.claude/

# Feedback for sibling crates (bug reports / feature requests; always internal — sent to their teams)
*_FEEDBACK.md

.DS_Store

# Zola build output
/site/public

# Secrets for one development machine, written by `just dev-keys > .env` (SR-142).
.env

# Copied from schemas/ when the site is built.
/site/static/schemas/
